  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 802.14 “Premark” means identifying the perimeter of the proposed site of an excavation by marking the perimeter in an appropriate manner in white paint, stakes, or other suitable white markings on non-paved surfaces. “Premark” also includes pink markings when winter conditions would render white premarkings not clearly visible.\n\nSource. #7350, eff 8-23-00; ss by #9226, INTERIM, eff 8-16-08, EXPIRES: 2-12-09; ss and moved by #9318, eff 11-8-08 (from Puc 802.13); ss by #12102, eff 2-8-17",
